Suppose $\widetilde{\rm I}$, $\widetilde{\rm II}$, $\widetilde{\rm III}$, $\widetilde{\rm IV}$ are those defined as \eqref{ffs} with respect to the other normal coordinates $(\widetilde{u},\widetilde{v})$. Then we have
\begin{gather}\label{invariant14}
